<!--Gem_Page_Main_Editor--><div class="clearfix"></div><div class="gryffeditor"><div data-label="Heading" id="e-1530778619646" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-id="1530778619646"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-center" data-gemlang="en"><h1 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2">Privacy policy</h1></div></div><!--gfsplit--><div class="element-wrap" data-label="Text Block" id="e-1530778473079" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-id="1530778473079"><div class="elm text-edit gf_gs-text-paragraph-1 gf-elm-left-lg gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs" data-exc=""><form id="form" method="post" novalidate="novalidate" action="/privacy-policy/"><div class="main js-main"><div class="main__inner"><div class="content js-content" style="min-height: 22px;"><div class="container container_text module module_middle  with-counter"><p><br></p><p><strong>Introduction&nbsp;</strong></p><p>We take your privacy very seriously and ask that you read this privacy policy</p><p>carefully. It contains important information on who we are, how and why we collect, store,</p><p>use, and share personal information, your rights in relation to your personal information,</p><p>and how to contact us and supervisory authorities if you have a complaint.</p><p><strong>Who We Are&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Study Active Limited, trading as Study Active in the UK, operates the website</p><p>www.studyactive.co.uk. We are the data controller of your personal information, as</p><p>defined by the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). We are regulated under GDPR,</p><p>which applies across the UK and the European Economic Area (EEA). Our designated</p><p>privacy officer is responsible for ensuring that we handle personal information in</p><p>accordance with the law. Contact details for our privacy officer are found in the "How to</p><p>Contact Us" section below.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Personal Information&nbsp;</strong><span style="font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;"><strong>We Collect and Use&nbsp;</strong></span></p><p><span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">We collect the following types of personal&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">information:</span></p><p>1. Personal information provided by you</p><p>2. When you interact with us, we collect personal information such as your name,</p><p>email address, phone number(s), date of birth, and postal address.</p><p>3. Personal information provided by third parties</p><p>Occasionally, we may receive information about you from third parties (such as credit</p><p>reference agencies) to help us provide services or improve your experience with us.</p><p>4. Personal information about other individuals</p><p>If you provide us with details about another person (e.g., a referee or next of kin), you</p><p>confirm that the individual has agreed to you sharing their personal data with us and to our</p><p>processing of their information as outlined in this policy.</p><p>5. Sensitive personal information</p><p>We generally do not collect sensitive personal data, but in some cases (e.g., healthrelated matters), we may request sensitive personal information with your explicit consent.</p><p>You may request deletion of such data at any time.</p><p>6. Children’s Data</p><p>We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 16. If we learn we have</p><p>collected data from a child under 16, we will delete that information immediately. Parents</p><p>or guardians may request access to or deletion of a child’s personal data.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>How and When We Collect Your Information&nbsp;</strong></p><p>We collect personal data when you:</p><p>• Visit our website, sign up for a course, or request course information</p><p>• Interact with us by phone, email, or in person at our gym locations</p><p>• Use cookies or submit information through website forms</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Cookies and Tracking Technologies&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Our website uses cookies to collect information that&nbsp;<span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">help improve your experience. For more details, please refer to our Cookie Policy. We</span></p><p>may also use cookies for targeted advertising. You can disable cookies in your browser&nbsp;<span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">settings, but this may affect some website features.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Reasons We Collect and Use Your Personal Information&nbsp;</strong></p><p>We process your personal data&nbsp;<span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">for several lawful bases under the GDPR, including:</span></p><p>• Contractual necessity</p><p>To provide you with the services you request, such as course enrollment, payments, and</p><p>certification.</p><p>• Legal obligations</p><p>To comply with laws such as anti-money laundering, fraud prevention, and counterterrorist financing.</p><p>• Legitimate interests</p><p>For activities such as improving services, customer research, fraud prevention, and</p><p>ensuring a secure environment at our gym facilities.</p><p>• Consent</p><p>For marketing communications, if we rely on your consent to send emails or SMS</p><p>messages, we will provide an easy way for you to opt-out.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Marketing Communications</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>We may use your personal information to send marketing&nbsp;<span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">communications about services we offer. You have the right to opt-out of receiving these</span></p><p>communications at any time by:</p><p>• Clicking the "unsubscribe" link in any marketing email</p><p>• Contacting us via email at info@studyactive.co.uk</p><p>• Opting out through our website when requesting course information</p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong>Credit Checking&nbsp;</strong></p><p>We may conduct credit checks on you for business purposes, such as&nbsp;<span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">verifying your ability to pay for services. We may also share your information with credit&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">reference agencies.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sharing Your Information&nbsp;</strong></p><p>We may share your personal information with the following:</p><p>• Service providers who assist in our business operations (e.g., payment processors,</p><p>fraud prevention)</p><p>• Law enforcement or regulatory authorities when required by law</p><p>• Third-party platforms for marketing purposes (with your consent)</p><p>• Other parties with whom we are negotiating a business transaction (e.g., sale of</p><p>business)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Security of Your Personal Information&nbsp;</strong></p><p>We implement reasonable physical, technical,</p><p>and organisational measures to protect your personal information, including:</p><p>• Secure servers and encrypted payment processing</p><p>• Limiting access to data to authorised personnel only</p><p>• Procedures to handle data breaches, including notifying you and the supervisory</p><p>authority when required by law</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Transfers Outside the EEA&nbsp;</strong></p><p>We do not transfer personal data outside the EEA. If we ever&nbsp;<span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">do, we will ensure appropriate safeguards are in place, such as Standard Contractual</span></p><p>Clauses, to protect your data.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Data Retention</strong></p><p>We will retain your personal information for no longer than necessary for</p><p>the purposes for which it was collected, in accordance with applicable UK law. In general,</p><p>we will retain data for 6 years from the end of our contract with you, unless you request</p><p>earlier deletion.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Your Rights Under GDPR</strong>, you have the following rights:</p><p>• Right to access: Request a copy of your personal data.</p><p>• Right to correction: Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</p><p>• Right to erasure: Request deletion of your personal data, in certain circumstances.</p><p>• Right to object: Object to the processing of your personal data for certain purposes.</p><p>• Right to restrict processing: Request limitation of processing in certain situations.</p><p>• Right to portability: Receive your data in a commonly used, machine-readable</p><p>format and transfer it to another data controller.</p><p><br></p><p>For further details on your rights or to exercise them, please contact us as per the "How to</p><p>Contact Us" section.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>How to Contact Us</strong></p><p>If you have any questions or concerns about this privacy policy, or if</p><p>you would like to exercise your rights, please contact us at:</p><p>Email: info@studyactive.co.uk</p><p>Address: Study Active Limited, Eastway Enterprise Centre, 7 Paynes Park, Hitchin, SG5&nbsp;<span style="font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;">1EH</span></p><p>Phone: 0345 017 8733</p><p><br></p><p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner’s Office</p><p>(ICO), the UK's supervisory authority for data protection, if you are dissatisfied with our</p><p>response. You can contact the ICO at www.ico.org.uk.</p><p>Changes to This Privacy Policy We may update this privacy policy periodically to reflect</p><p>changes in our practices or legal requirements. Please review this policy regularly to stay</p><p>informed.</p><p><br></p><p>This policy was last updated on 15th March 2025.</p></div></div></div></div></form></div></div><!--gfsplit--><script>window.__gemStoreData = {};window.__gemStoreData.gemKeyValid = {};window.__gemStoreData.gemKeyValid.bestWayAddToCart = 1;</script></div><div id="divContentBk"></div><!--End_Gem_Page_Main_Editor-->
